.TH START-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-CHAIN.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh \- bring up the full public path: EC2 proxy, Caddy, reverse tunnel, local server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/start\-mu2edaq\-notify\-chain.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts and verifies, in eight logged steps, the chain
phone \(-> EC2 Caddy \(-> SSH reverse tunnel \(-> local
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1).
Every step is idempotent, so the script also serves as a repair:
.IP 1. 4
Start the EC2 instance if stopped (waiting out
.BR stopping ),
then wait for
.B instance\-running
and
.BR instance\-status\-ok .
.IP 2. 4
Read this start's public IPv4 from the EC2 API (the instance has no Elastic
IP). If Route 53 does not already hold it, wait for the instance's own
updater, then publish it from here with
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1)
unless
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_LOCAL_FALLBACK=0 .
A stale local resolver answer is only a warning.
.IP 3. 4
Wait for SSH to the instance.
.IP 4. 4
.B systemctl start caddy
on the instance and require it to be active.
.IP 5. 4
Start the reverse tunnel
.RB ( "ssh \-N \-R" ,
.BR ExitOnForwardFailure=yes ,
30 s keepalives) under
.BR nohup (1)
unless one is already bound on the instance.
.IP 6. 4
Start the local server with
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1)
unless
.B LOCAL_HEALTH_URL
already answers 200, then wait up to 40 s for health.
.IP 7. 4
From the instance, fetch
.B /api/health
through the tunnel.
.IP 8. 4
Wait up to 40 s for the public
.B /api/health
to answer.
.PP
Neither the tunnel nor a server started in step 6 is supervised. If the
server had been running under its launchd agent and was stopped by
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1),
this script does not re\-load the agent.
.SH OPTIONS
None; everything is set by environment variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scripts/notify-proxy-common.sh
Shared defaults: instance id, region, DNS name, Route 53 zone, TTL, wait
counts.
.TP
.I data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy.pem
SSH key for the instance (default; forced to mode 600).
.TP
.IR data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy-tunnel.pid ", " data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy-tunnel.log
Tunnel pid and log.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_INSTANCE_ID ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_REGION ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_DNS_NAME ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ROUTE53_ZONE_ID
Which instance, region, public name and hosted zone; defaults in
.IR scripts/notify-proxy-common.sh .
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_HOST
Address to use when the EC2 API reports none.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_USER ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_KEY
SSH user (default
.BR ec2\-user )
and key file.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_REMOTE_BIND ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_LOCAL_TARGET
Tunnel ends (defaults
.B 127.0.0.1:18095
on the instance,
.B 127.0.0.1:8095
locally).
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_PIDFILE ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_LOGFILE
Tunnel pid and log paths.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PUBLIC_URL
Public base URL; step 8 checks it with
.B /api/health
appended (default
.BR https://$MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_DNS_NAME ).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_LOCAL_HEALTH_URL
Full local health URL checked in step 6 (default
.BR https://127.0.0.1:8095/api/health ,
fetched without certificate verification).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_LOCAL_FALLBACK
0 disables publishing the A record from this host in step 2.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_SSH_WAIT_TRIES
SSH attempts, 5 s apart (default 36).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DEBUG
1 enables
.BR "set \-x" .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when the public endpoint answers. 1 on the first failed check, after
printing local and remote diagnostics to stderr. An
.B aws
command that fails outside a check (for example an
.B aws ec2 wait
timeout in step 1) ends the script with that command's own status under
.BR "set \-e" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scripts/start\-mu2edaq\-notify\-chain.sh
scripts/status\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1),
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1),
.BR status-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1),
.BR restore-mu2edaq-notify-tunnel.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1)
.PP
.IR docs/application-chain.md ,
.I docs/reverse-proxy-operations.md
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
